# 13. AI OPPONENT SYSTEM

The opponent must be controlled entirely by local TypeScript AI logic.

Do not use Gemini API calls or external AI services during gameplay.

Create three difficulty levels:

### EASY

- Slower reaction time.
- Less aggressive.
- Frequently makes mistakes.
- Blocks occasionally.
- Uses fewer special attacks.

### MEDIUM

- Balanced reaction time.
- Uses combinations.
- Blocks and dodges.
- Maintains attack distance.
- Uses special attacks intelligently.

### HARD

- Faster reaction time.
- Better positioning.
- More effective blocking.
- Uses dodging.
- Combines attacks.
- Recognises opportunities.
- Uses special attacks strategically.

### AI finite state machine

Implement these states:

- IDLE
- APPROACH
- RETREAT
- ATTACK
- BLOCK
- DODGE
- JUMP
- SPECIAL
- RECOVER

The AI should make decisions based on:

- Distance between fighters.
- Player health.
- AI health.
- Stamina.
- Energy.
- Attack cooldowns.
- Current combat state.
- Recent player attacks.
- Difficulty setting.

Include realistic reaction delays.

The AI must not read future player inputs or cheat by reacting instantly to every action.

AI must work completely offline.

